{"pageid": 899, "title": "White Mask", "revid": 2777, "categories": ["Lore", "Masks", "Monster hunters", "Order of St. George", "White Masks"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/5/52/White_Mask.png/revision/latest?cb=20241130215853\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"The White Mask of the North American Houses.\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"98\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" data-image-name=\"White Mask.png\" data-image-key=\"White_Mask.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/5/52/White_Mask.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241130215853\" /></a> \t<noscript><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/5/52/White_Mask.png/revision/latest?cb=20241130215853\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"The White Mask of the North American Houses.\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/5/52/White_Mask.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241130215853\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"98\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"White Mask.png\" data-image-key=\"White_Mask.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/5/52/White_Mask.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241130215853\" /></a></noscript> \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:White_Mask.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t\t\t<p class=\"caption\">The White Mask of the North American Houses.</p> \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border-style:none; background-color:transparent;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"top\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;padding:10px 10px;\">“\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\"><i>We are a </i>faction of--<i> not a </i>totem to--<i> the Order! Once in the </i>Americas,<i> I will rally a </i>new<i> team, selected by </i>my<i> hand from </i>promising émigré,<i> already proven eager to abandon their identities in favor of a </i>paragon of tenacity.<i> And they will be... </i>will only ever have been White Masks.<b></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"bottom\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:right;padding:10px 10px;\">”\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\"><div style=\"line-height:1em;text-align: right\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal;\">&#8212; <span class=\"new\" title=\"Father Alabaster Cutter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRmF0aGVyX0FsYWJhc3Rlcl9DdXR0ZXI/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Father Alabaster Cutter</span>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"House of Slaughter 16 (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSG91c2Vfb2ZfU2xhdWdodGVyXzE2P2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\"><i>House of Slaughter</i> #16</span></cite></div><i></i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><b>White Masks</b> are a branch of <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">The Order of St. George</a> who don the color white and hunt <a href=\"/wiki/Monsters\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Monsters\">monsters</a> as a group. Often compared to packs of wolves, they are trained to take down large monsters as a team in order to minimize loss of life. They are usually known to have rivalries with the solo-hunting <a href=\"/wiki/Black_Masks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Black Masks\">Black Masks</a>, and in contrast to them are usually the largest branch of any given House. Despite this, they are often remarked to be cruel and callous.\n</p><p>The term \"White Mask\" is mainly used in the Americas, after Father Alabaster of the Cutters declared his settlement to be White Masks. In Europe, this branch is more often the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Alabaster Masks (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQWxhYmFzdGVyX01hc2tzP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Alabaster Masks</span>, who are known for choosing promising members from the other houses and training them as expert hunters.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS16&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS16-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border-style:none; background-color:transparent;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"top\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;padding:10px 10px;\">“\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\"><i>White Masks are typically the largest branch of each House, requiring the most recruits. They are pack hunters, trained to work together as a unit to bring down the largest monsters the Order faces in its work.</i>\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"bottom\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:right;padding:10px 10px;\">”\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\"><div style=\"line-height:1em;text-align: right\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal;\">&#8212; <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Slaughter_1\" title=\"Book of Slaughter 1\">The Book of Slaughter</a></i></cite></div><i></i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The White Masks are the pack hunters of the Order. They are trained in multiple hunting techniques, with a specific focus on teamwork, strategy, and group attacks. With larger groups of hunters being used to take down larger monsters, they sometimes end up with a bit of an ego due to how impressive their kills can be; despite this, many often flounder when left alone.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC20&#95;2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC20-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Because of this, many easily pass <span class=\"new\" title=\"The Sacrament of the Hunt (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVGhlX1NhY3JhbWVudF9vZl90aGVfSHVudD9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">the Sacrament of the Hunt</span>, as they are allowed to hunt in their usual team, but have a high mortality rate during <span class=\"new\" title=\"The Sacrament of Trepanation (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVGhlX1NhY3JhbWVudF9vZl9UcmVwYW5hdGlvbj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">the Blind Hunt</span>, where they are expected to operate completely alone.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOS&#95;3-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOS-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>Group Hunters are expected to take down larger monsters on their own, while smaller monsters are taken down by Black or Silver Masks. The White Masks are often also used for larger cover-ups and assassinations, such as when large amounts of people witness a monster attack.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC11&#95;4-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC11-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> \n</p><p>Despite being raised to be reliant on their team and in being the biggest branch of each House, White Masks are often socially aggressive, prideful, and violent.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC13&#95;5-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC13-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> Most other branches have a dislike for them, which results in White Masks becoming more reliant on each other than other hunters.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-SIKTC20&#95;2-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-SIKTC20-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>The branch was originally born in the 1600s-1700s, when the colonization of America first began. <span class=\"new\" title=\"Father Alabaster Cutter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRmF0aGVyX0FsYWJhc3Rlcl9DdXR0ZXI/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Father Alabaster Cutter</span> of the <span class=\"new\" title=\"House of Cutter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSG91c2Vfb2ZfQ3V0dGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">House of Cutter</span> decided to emigrate to the colonies himself, rather than send members of his team, and argued that the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Alabaster Masks (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQWxhYmFzdGVyX01hc2tzP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Alabasters'</span> way of fighting deserved its own identity, rather than being considered rejects from other houses.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS16&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS16-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Known_White_Masks\">Known White Masks</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Early_Days_of_America\">Early Days of America</span></h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Father Alabaster Cutter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRmF0aGVyX0FsYWJhc3Rlcl9DdXR0ZXI/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Father Alabaster Cutter</span> †</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"House_of_Boucher\"><span class=\"new\" title=\"House of Boucher (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSG91c2Vfb2ZfQm91Y2hlcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">House of Boucher</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Jolie Boucher (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSm9saWVfQm91Y2hlcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Jolie Boucher</span> <small>(leader)</small></li></ul>\n<p><span class=\"new\" title=\"Jace Boucher (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSmFjZV9Cb3VjaGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Jace Boucher</span> and his family were White Masks; after the fall of the Boucher family, Jace first transferred to the <a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Slaughter\" title=\"House of Slaughter\">House of Slaughter</a> and then defected entirely.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS1&#95;6-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS1-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> His adoptive son, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Sunny Boucher (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvU3VubnlfQm91Y2hlcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Sunny Boucher</span>, would temporarily join, only to escape while the rest of his siblings were captured by Jolie.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS25&#95;7-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS25-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"House_of_Slaughter\"><a href=\"/wiki/House_of_Slaughter\" title=\"House of Slaughter\">House of Slaughter</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Cecilia_Slaughter\" title=\"Cecilia Slaughter\">Cecilia Slaughter</a> <small>(leader)</small></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Helen Slaughter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGVsZW5fU2xhdWdodGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Helen Slaughter</span> †</li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Paris Slaughter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUGFyaXNfU2xhdWdodGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Paris Slaughter</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Tybalt Slaughter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVHliYWx0X1NsYXVnaHRlcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Tybalt Slaughter</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Maple Slaughter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTWFwbGVfU2xhdWdodGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Maple Slaughter</span> †<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS27&#95;8-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS27-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Marco Slaughter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTWFyY29fU2xhdWdodGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Marco Slaughter</span><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS28&#95;9-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS28-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Bait Slaughter (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQmFpdF9TbGF1Z2h0ZXI/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Bait Slaughter</span> <small>(transferred to <a href=\"/wiki/Silver_Mask\" title=\"Silver Mask\">Silver Mask</a>)</small></li></ul>\n<p><span class=\"new\" title=\"Jace Boucher (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSmFjZV9Cb3VjaGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Jace Boucher</span> served as a transfer from the House of Boucher, and lived as Jace Slaughter for some time before defecting and escaping the house.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS5&#95;10-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS5-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> <a href=\"/wiki/Maxine_Slaughter\" title=\"Maxine Slaughter\">Maxine Slaughter</a> was originally a high-ranking White Mask before her transfer to the <a href=\"/wiki/Black_Masks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Black Masks\">Black Masks</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<div id=\"ga